    "category_name": "Excel & Spreadsheets",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Explore the Excel workspace, the Ribbon tabs, Quick Access Toolbar, Formula Bar, and Status Bar.",
    "content": "# Lesson 01: Introduction to Excel & The Ribbon Interface\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 01** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Excel Curriculum! In this first lesson, you will master the foundational layout of Microsoft Excel so you feel 100% confident navigating the software.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is Microsoft Excel?\nMicrosoft Excel is an electronic spreadsheet application used worldwide to store, organize, calculate, analyze, and visualize data.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Anatomy of the Excel Screen\nWhen you launch Excel, you are presented with several core areas:\n- **Title Bar**: Shows your workbook name (e.g., \\`Book1.xlsx\\`) and search box.\n- **The Ribbon**: The control center containing commands organized into logical **Tabs** (*Home, Insert, Page Layout, Formulas, Data, Review, View*).\n- **Ribbon Groups**: Within each tab, commands are grouped together (e.g., Font, Alignment, Number).\n- **Name Box**: Located on the left above the grid, displaying the active cell address (e.g., \\`A1\\`).\n- **Formula Bar**: The long input box where you enter and edit cell contents or formulas.\n- **The Worksheet Grid**: Millions of individual cells arranged in columns and rows.\n- **Sheet Tabs**: Located at the bottom left to switch between multiple worksheets.\n- **Status Bar**: Located at the very bottom, showing view modes, zoom controls, and quick statistics (*Average, Count, Sum* of highlighted cells).\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Keyboard Shortcut**: Press \\`Ctrl + F1\\` on your keyboard to instantly collapse or expand the Excel Ribbon to maximize your screen space!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Open a blank Excel workbook.\n2. Click through each Ribbon tab (*Home, Insert, Formulas, Data*) and notice how commands are grouped.\n3. Click into cell \\`C5\\` and check if the **Name Box** displays \\`C5\\`.\n4. Type \\`Welcome to Bargisy eSchool\\` into the Formula Bar and press \\`Enter\\`.\n",
