    "title": "Lesson 07: Number Formatting: Currency, Percentages, Decimals, and Dates",
    "slug": "lesson-07-number-formatting-currency,-percentages,-decimals,-and-dates",
    "category": "excel",
    "category_name": "Excel & Spreadsheets",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Ensure numbers display their true meaning with currency symbols, decimal precision, and standard date formats.",
    "content": "# Lesson 07: Number Formatting: Currency, Percentages & Dates\n\nIn Excel, the **actual value** stored in a cell can look completely different from the **displayed value** on your screen.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Common Number Formats\n\n| Format Type | Raw Number Stored | Formatted Display | Shortcut |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **General** | \\`1500\\` | \\`1500\\` | \\`Ctrl + Shift + ~\\`, |\n| **Currency** | \\`1500\\` | \\`$1,500.00\\` | \\`Ctrl + Shift + $\\` |\n| **Percentage** | \\`0.85\\` | \\`85%\\` | \\`Ctrl + Shift + %\\` |\n| **Date** | \\`46336\\` | \\`2026-11-10\\` | \\`Ctrl + Shift + #\\` |\n| **Number** | \\`1500\\` | \\`1,500.00\\` | \\`Ctrl + Shift + !\\` |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Increasing & Decreasing Decimal Precision\nOn the **Home tab** in the **Number group**, use the two decimal icons:\n- **Increase Decimal**: Displays more decimal places (\\`$15.2\\` -> \\`$15.20\\`).\n- **Decrease Decimal**: Rounds the visual display to fewer decimals.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Decreasing decimals only changes how the number looks! The full unrounded precision is still used in formula calculations!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Type \\`0.175\\` into cell \\`B2\\`.\n2. Apply Percentage format. Notice it displays \\`18%\\`.\n3. Click \"Increase Decimal\" once. Notice it now displays the accurate \\`17.5%\\`!\n",
