    "title": "Lesson 09: Inserting, Deleting, Renaming, and Color-Coding Worksheets",
    "slug": "lesson-09-inserting,-deleting,-renaming,-and-color-coding-worksheets",
    "category": "excel",
    "category_name": "Excel & Spreadsheets",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Organize complex workbooks with structured sheet tabs, tab colors, and proper sheet management.",
    "content": "# Lesson 09: Managing Worksheets: Insert, Rename, Color & Move\n\nAs your models grow, keeping all your data on a single messy worksheet creates confusion. Professional workbooks use dedicated sheets for Inputs, Calculations, and Reports.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Sheet Management Actions\n- **Insert New Sheet**: Click the circle **\\`+\\`** button next to existing sheet tabs, or press \\`Shift + F11\\`.\n- **Rename Sheet**: Double-click the sheet tab, type the new name (e.g., \\`2026_Sales\\`), and press \\`Enter\\`.\n- **Tab Color**: Right-click the tab -> **Tab Color** -> Pick a visual color (e.g., Green for Revenue, Red for Expenses).\n- **Reorder Sheets**: Click and drag any sheet tab left or right to reorder.\n- **Duplicate Sheet**: Hold \\`Ctrl\\` while dragging a sheet tab to create an instant exact copy!\n\n---\n\n## 2. Worksheet Naming Rules\n- Sheet names cannot exceed **31 characters**.\n- Cannot contain characters: \\`/\\`, \\`\\\\`, \\`?\\`, \\`*\\`, \\`:\\`, \\`[\\`, or \\`]\\`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. Rename \\`Sheet1\\` to \\`Summary\\`.\n2. Insert 2 new sheets and rename them \\`Data_Input\\` and \\`Calculations\\`.\n3. Set the \\`Summary\\` tab color to Dark Blue and \\`Data_Input\\` to Emerald Green.\n4. Drag \\`Summary\\` so it is the first tab on the left.\n",
