    "title": "Lesson 11: The Power of AutoFill: Numbers, Dates, and Custom Lists",
    "slug": "lesson-11-the-power-of-autofill-numbers,-dates,-and-custom-lists",
    "category": "excel",
    "category_name": "Excel & Spreadsheets",
    "difficulty": "Beginner",
    "summary": "Automate repetitive typing with Excel's AutoFill handle for sequential numbers, dates, and patterns.",
    "content": "# Lesson 11: The Power of AutoFill\n\nTyping repetitive sequences like days of the week, months, or consecutive invoice numbers manually is a waste of time. **AutoFill** does it in half a second.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What is the AutoFill Handle?\nSelect any cell. Notice the tiny square dot at the bottom-right corner of the green border. That is the **Fill Handle**.\nWhen your mouse hovers over it, the cursor turns into a thin black plus sign (\\`+\\`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. AutoFill Behaviors\n- **Months**: Type \\`January\\`, drag the fill handle down -> Excel automatically fills *February, March, April...*\n- **Days of Week**: Type \\`Monday\\`, drag -> fills *Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday...*\n- **Dates**: Type \\`2026-01-01\\`, drag -> fills consecutive calendar dates.\n- **Number Sequences**:\n  - If you type \\`1\\` and drag, Excel copies \\`1, 1, 1...\\`\n  - To count up: Type \\`1\\` in cell A1, type \\`2\\` in cell A2. Select **both** cells, then drag down. Excel recognizes the step pattern and fills \\`3, 4, 5, 6...\\`!\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Double-Click Magic**: If you have a column of data on the left, simply **double-click** the fill handle to autofill all the way down to the bottom of the table automatically!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\n1. In cell \\`A1\\`, type \\`Invoice-001\\`.\n2. Drag the fill handle down 10 rows. Notice how Excel intelligently increments to \\`Invoice-010\\`!\n3. In cell \\`B1\\`, type \\`Q1-2026\\` and drag down 8 rows.\n",
    "tags": "Excel, Lesson 11, Fundamentals, Beginner",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 346,
